        <record id="remotecontrol_avamet" model="remotecontrol">
            <field name="name">Web AVAMET</field>
            <field name="remotecontrol_type">rest</field>
            <field name="base_url">https://api.weatherlink.com/v2</field>
            <field name="timeout">30</field>
            <field name="verify_ssl">True</field>
            <field name="rate_limit_seconds">0.0</field>
            <field name="max_retries">1</field>
            <field name="backoff">1.5</field>
            <field name="readonly">True</field>
            <field name="is_avamet">True</field>
            <field name="connection_params">{"api_key": "", "api_secret": ""}</field>
            <field name="remotecontrol_help"><![CDATA[
<h2>AVAMET WeatherLink · Odoo Integration</h2>

<hr/>

<h3>1) Connection (Remote Control)</h3>
<p>Type: <code>REST</code></p>
<p>Base URL: <code>https://api.weatherlink.com/v2</code></p>
<p><strong>connection_params</strong> (JSON):</p>
<pre>{
    "api_key": "your_api_key",
    "api_secret": "your_api_secret"
}</pre>
<ul>
    <li>All requests include query param <code>api-key</code>.</li>
    <li>All requests include header <code>x-api-secret</code>.</li>
    <li>Retries with backoff are applied for timeout, connection errors, HTTP 429 and HTTP 5xx.</li>
</ul>

<h3>2) Device And Sensor Configuration</h3>
<p>Use the button <strong>AVAMET Stations</strong> to load the available stations and discover the real variables returned by the API.</p>
<p>The wizard creates one device per station and lets you select the discovered API fields as sensors.</p>
<p>Each created device stores in <strong>remotecontrol_params</strong> a JSON like:</p>
<pre>{
    "station_id": "001D0A71B1CA",
    "station_name": "BOVALAR",
    "start_date": "2026-06-28"
}</pre>
<p>Each sensor stores in <strong>remotecontrol_params</strong> a JSON like:</p>
<pre>{
    "api_field": "rainfall_mm",
    "start_date": "2026-06-28"
}</pre>
<ul>
    <li><code>station_id</code>: WeatherLink station identifier used in API calls.</li>
    <li><code>station_name</code>: descriptive station name.</li>
    <li><code>start_date</code>: optional first date for the initial import.</li>
    <li><code>api_field</code>: exact WeatherLink field stored in the sensor.</li>
</ul>

<h3>3) Available Procedure</h3>
<p>The module includes the procedure <strong>AVAMET: Daily Sync</strong>.</p>
<ol>
    <li><strong>Get devices (plan)</strong> → builds <code>bag["sensors_plan"]</code> from configured Odoo devices and sensors.</li>
    <li><strong>Get readings</strong> → calls WeatherLink historic endpoints and upserts readings in <code>mdm.measurement.device.sensor.reading</code>.</li>
</ol>

<h3>4) API Endpoints Used</h3>
<ul>
    <li><strong>GET /stations</strong> → loads the station catalog in the import wizard.</li>
    <li><strong>GET /stations/&lt;station_id&gt;</strong> → retrieves station metadata during device creation.</li>
    <li><strong>GET /historic/&lt;station_id&gt;</strong> → retrieves historical data for each configured magnitude.</li>
</ul>

<p>Historical requests are executed in 6-hour windows and aggregated into one daily value per sensor and day.</p>
            ]]></field>
        </record>

        <record id="remotecontrol_avamet_action_get_devices" model="remotecontrol.action">
            <field name="name">AVAMET: Get devices (plan)</field>
            <field name="remote_id" ref="remotecontrol_avamet"/>
            <field name="active">True</field>
            <field name="rate_limit_seconds">0.0</field>
            <field name="max_retries">1</field>
            <field name="backoff">0</field>
            <field name="readonly">True</field>
            <field name="code"><![CDATA[
plan = self.remote_id.avamet_get_sensor_plan(selected_device_ids)
bag['sensors_plan'] = plan
            ]]></field>
        </record>

        <record id="remotecontrol_avamet_action_get_readings" model="remotecontrol.action">
            <field name="name">AVAMET: Get readings</field>
            <field name="remote_id" ref="remotecontrol_avamet"/>
            <field name="active">True</field>
            <field name="rate_limit_seconds">0.0</field>
            <field name="max_retries">1</field>
            <field name="backoff">0</field>
            <field name="readonly">True</field>
            <field name="code"><![CDATA[
plan = bag.get('sensors_plan') or []
audit = self.remote_id.avamet_sync_sensor_plan(plan)
bag['upserts'] = audit.get('total_upserts', 0)
bag['errors'] = audit.get('total_errors', 0)
bag['audit_attachment_id'] = audit.get('attachment_id')
            ]]></field>
        </record>

        <record id="remotecontrol_avamet_procedure" model="remotecontrol.procedure">
            <field name="name">AVAMET: Daily Sync</field>
            <field name="remote_id" ref="remotecontrol_avamet"/>
            <field name="active">True</field>
            <field name="readonly">True</field>
            <field name="procedure_for_readings">True</field>
        </record>

        <record id="remotecontrol_avamet_step_10_devices" model="remotecontrol.step">
            <field name="name">Get devices (plan)</field>
            <field name="procedure_id" ref="remotecontrol_avamet_procedure"/>
            <field name="action_id" ref="remotecontrol_avamet_action_get_devices"/>
            <field name="sequence">10</field>
        </record>

        <record id="remotecontrol_avamet_step_20_readings" model="remotecontrol.step">
            <field name="name">Get readings</field>
            <field name="procedure_id" ref="remotecontrol_avamet_procedure"/>
            <field name="action_id" ref="remotecontrol_avamet_action_get_readings"/>
            <field name="sequence">20</field>
        </record>

